### What is the time and space complexity?

Time is **O(N)**: prefix computation is O(N) and each deque operation is amortized O(1). Space is **O(N)** for the prefix array and the deque.

### How does this compare to the positive-only variant?

| Variant | Array type | Algorithm | Time | Space |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Positive only | All positive | Sliding window | O(N) | O(1) |
| With negatives | Mixed signs | Prefix + deque | O(N) | O(N) |

Recognizing when the simple window fails and reaching for prefix sums plus a monotonic deque is the real signal of depth.

### What should a senior engineer know?

A senior engineer should understand these deeper aspects.

- **The dual pop is the core invariant**: front pops handle qualification, back pops handle domination. Being able to articulate both is what proves understanding.
- **Use long for prefix sums**: monetary data can overflow int across many transactions.
- **The positive-only window is a special case**: when all elements are positive, the deque degenerates into a simple two-pointer because prefix sums are already monotonically increasing.
- **Related problems**: sliding window maximum/minimum also use monotonic deques but for different invariants.
